  "summary_md": "Today’s batch splits between traditional energy services under strain and a growing set of names riding defense modernization, AI infrastructure buildout, and data-driven service shifts. Standout momentum is visible at DAKT (record orders and backlog), MPTI (defense backlog swelling toward ambitious growth targets), NGS (rental compression hitting new highs), and FTK, where a data‑analytics pivot has driven consecutive guidance raises. Pressure points include CLB’s margin erosion and earnings miss with no clear mitigation, and NCSM’s revenue decline that triggered a wave of downgrades. Transformational moves dominate elsewhere: DAIO is doubling its size via acquisition while introducing a recurring service model, KOPN entered AI optical interconnects through a Fabric.AI partnership, and OPTX used an equity raise to fix liquidity and secure defense wearable‑optics contracts. A cross‑cutting anomaly is the intrusion of crypto and AI‑storage narratives into industrial coverage—FET, LINK, and SND are trading on token adoption or AI‑memory demand rather than legacy operations—highlighting a market eager to reprice anything AI‑adjacent.",
